# Error Handling

## Custom Exceptions

Use focused exception classes instead of a single DomainError. This integrates cleanly with Spring's `@ControllerAdvice`.

```java
// src/main/java/com/duoc/LearningPlatform/exception/ResourceNotFoundException.java

public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {

    public ResourceNotFoundException(String resourceName, Long id) {
        super(resourceName + " with id " + id + " not found");
    }

    public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
```

## Global Exception Handler

A single `@RestControllerAdvice` class maps exceptions to HTTP responses for the entire application.

```java
// src/main/java/com/duoc/LearningPlatform/exception/GlobalExceptionHandler.java

import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.http.ResponseEntity;
import org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

import java.util.Map;
import java.util.stream.Collectors;

@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> handleNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                .body(Map.of("error", ex.getMessage()));
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(IllegalArgumentException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> handleBadRequest(IllegalArgumentException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
                .body(Map.of("error", ex.getMessage()));
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(IllegalStateException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> handleBusinessRule(IllegalStateException ex) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY)
                .body(Map.of("error", ex.getMessage()));
    }

    @ExceptionHandler(MethodArgumentNotValidException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> handleValidation(MethodArgumentNotValidException ex) {
        String message = ex.getBindingResult().getFieldErrors().stream()
                .map(e -> e.getField() + ": " + e.getDefaultMessage())
                .collect(Collectors.joining(", "));
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
                .body(Map.of("error", message));
    }
}
```

---

## Which Exception to Use

| Situation | Exception | HTTP Status |
|-----------|-----------|-------------|
| Entity not found | `ResourceNotFoundException` | 404 |
| Invalid input / validation | `IllegalArgumentException` | 400 |
| Bean Validation failure (`@Valid`) | `MethodArgumentNotValidException` | 400 |
| Business rule violation | `IllegalStateException` | 422 |
| Unexpected / technical | Let bubble up | 500 |

---

## Where to Throw

### In Model (invariants)

```java
public void confirm() {
    if (this.items.isEmpty()) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot confirm an empty order");
    }
    this.status = OrderStatus.CONFIRMED;
}
```

### In Service (not found, business rules)

```java
public Order getOrder(Long id) {
    return orderRepository.findById(id)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new ResourceNotFoundException("Order", id));
}
```

### In Controller — NOTHING

Controllers don't handle errors directly. The `GlobalExceptionHandler` does it.

